      "Language": "cze",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Mycotic aneurysm of the coronary artery occurs in less than 1% of patients with infective endocarditis and only few cases of successful treatment has been described in the literature. The paper presents a case of 64 years old man with infective endocarditis of the mitral valve, complicated with a development of mycotic aneurysm of the right coronary artery, who was successfully surgically treated."},
